namespace RoundTrip.V10_7

/-- The project's statement (universes instantiated at `0`). `retr` (Milnor's `r_u`: on `[0, tᵢ]`
the broken geodesic of the break points of `γ`, on `[tᵢ, u]` the short geodesic from `γ(tᵢ)` to
`γ(u)`, `γ` on `[u, 1]`) and `deform` (`retr` on `[0, 1]`, `γ` off `[0, 1]`, the identity outside
`[0, 1] × Int Ω^c`) are definitions (vocabulary); the theorems are `E(r_u γ) ≤ E(γ)`, `r_u`
fixes broken geodesics on `[0, 1]`, and joint continuity of `(u, γ) ↦ r_u(γ)` on
`[0, 1] × Int Ω^c` for Milnor's metric. -/
def A : Prop :=
  type_of% @Morse.BrokenSetup.energy_retr_le.{0,0,0} ∧
    type_of% @Morse.BrokenSetup.retr_of_mem_brokenPaths.{0,0,0} ∧
    type_of% @Morse.BrokenSetup.continuousOn_deform.{0,0,0}

theorem A_holds : A :=
  ⟨@Morse.BrokenSetup.energy_retr_le, @Morse.BrokenSetup.retr_of_mem_brokenPaths,
    @Morse.BrokenSetup.continuousOn_deform⟩

/-! Neither direction is proved (see `V10_7.json`).

* `A → B` fails genuinely: B quantifies over abstract connected Hausdorff `ℝⁿ`-manifolds with any
  smooth metric and any Levi-Civita connection; A only concerns slice submanifolds `N ⊆ V` with the
  induced metric (the project has no abstract geodesics, `exp`, or path spaces).
* `B → A` fails genuinely: A is about the project's specific maps `retr`/`deform`; B only asserts
  that *some* `r`, `r_u` with Milnor's listed properties exist, so it says nothing about `retr`.
  (Conversely B lists properties not among A's theorems: `r(ω) ∈ B`, `r_0 = id`, `r_1 = r` —
  `deform_one_mem_brokenPaths`, `retr_zero`, `retr_one` in the project, outside this item — and
  the three-piece description, which in the project is the definition `retrSeg`.)

## The embedded special case

`B_emb` is B for `M = ↥N` (`Bridge.Sub hN`) with the induced connection (`B_to_B_emb`). Even
there, `A → B_emb` would need more than dictionary glue: the hypotheses differ. B's data
(`Setup16`: `ε` with the conclusion of Lemma 10.8 on `S = {ρ(p, ·) ≤ √c}`, `ShortGood`, and
`t_{i+1} − tᵢ < ε²/c`) do not provide a `Morse.BrokenSetup` with `δ = ε`: the project also asks
that `δ` be at most a normal radius at every point of `S` (`BrokenSetup.normal`), that
Corollary 10.8 hold with minimality and a smooth local representative on an *open* neighbourhood
in `V × V` (`IsShortJoin`), and that `S` be compact. The normal-radius condition does not follow
from `ShortGood` (on the unit sphere with `S` a small cap, `ShortGood S ε` holds for some
`ε > π`, beyond the conjugate radius); with a smaller `δ` the fineness condition
`c (t_{i+1} − tᵢ) < δ²` may fail for B's subdivision. Besides, one would need the dictionary
between the blind `Ω` (functions `ℝ → ↥N`, topology generated by `d`-balls) and
`Morse.PathSp N p q` (Milnor's metric: `Items/V10_1.lean`, `Emb.edist_eq`), and between the blind
`B` (geodesic on each closed `[tᵢ, t_{i+1}]`) and `BrokenSetup.brokenPaths` (geodesic on each open
`(tᵢ, t_{i+1})`, piecewise smooth). -/

/-- **B on embedded manifolds**: `M = ↥N` (`Bridge.Sub hN`, model `ℝⁿ`, induced metric) with the
induced Levi-Civita connection `Bridge.conn`. -/
def B_emb : Prop :=
  ∀ (V : Type) [NormedAddCommGroup V] [InnerProductSpace ℝ V] [FiniteDimensional ℝ V]
    (W : Type) [NormedAddCommGroup W] [NormedSpace ℝ W] [FiniteDimensional ℝ W] (n : ℕ)
    (N : Set V) (hN : Milnor.IsSliceSubmanifold 𝓘(ℝ, V) (Rn n) W N)
    [ConnectedSpace (Bridge.Sub hN)], MetricComplete n (Bridge.Sub hN) →
    ∀ (p q : Bridge.Sub hN) (c ε : ℝ) (k : ℕ) (t : ℕ → ℝ),
      Setup16 n (Bridge.conn (hN := hN)) p q c ε k t →
      ∃ (r : Om n p q → Om n p q) (R : unitInterval → Om n p q → Om n p q),
        IsRetr16 n (Bridge.conn (hN := hN)) p q c ε k t r R

theorem B_to_B_emb : B → B_emb := fun hB _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ n _ hN _ =>
  hB n (Bridge.Sub hN) (Bridge.conn (hN := hN)) Bridge.conn_isLC

end RoundTrip.V10_7
